**user**:
> Is there a closed form expression for sum_0..T exp(b t)?
**assistant**:
> For integer $T \ge 0$,
> 
> \[
> \sum_{t=0}^{T} e^{bt}
> =
> \frac{e^{b(T+1)}-1}{e^b-1},
> \qquad b \ne 0.
> \]
> 
> When $b=0$, every term is $1$, so
> 
> \[
> \sum_{t=0}^{T} e^{bt} = T+1.
> \]
> 
> A numerically convenient equivalent form (especially for small $b$) is
> 
> \[
> \sum_{t=0}^{T} e^{bt}
> =
> e^{bT/2}\,
> \frac{\sinh\!\left(b(T+1)/2\right)}{\sinh(b/2)}.
> \]
